For the 10.20260901 release, the two errors are

```
[ 41 of 757] Compiling Utility.Hash.Crypton ( Utility/Hash/Crypton.hs, dist/build/git-annex/git-annex-tmp/Utility/Hash/Crypton.dyn_o )

Utility/Hash/Crypton.hs:227:27: error: [GHC-39999]
    • No instance for ‘BA.ByteArrayAccess (Digest a)’
        arising from a use of ‘BA.convert’
    • In the second argument of ‘(.)’, namely ‘BA.convert’
      In the expression: HashDigest . BA.convert
      In an equation for ‘hashDigest’:
          hashDigest = HashDigest . BA.convert
    |
227 | hashDigest = HashDigest . BA.convert
    |                           ^^^^^^^^^^
```
and
```
[187 of 757] Compiling Annex.Balanced   ( Annex/Balanced.hs, dist/build/git-annex/git-annex-tmp/Annex/Balanced.dyn_o )

Annex/Balanced.hs:39:19: error: [GHC-39999]
    • No instance for ‘BA.ByteArrayAccess (Digest a)’
        arising from a use of ‘BA.unpack’
    • In the second argument of ‘(.)’, namely ‘BA.unpack’
      In the expression:
        L.foldl' (\ i b -> (i `shiftL` 8) + fromIntegral b) 0 . BA.unpack
      In an equation for ‘tointeger’:
          tointeger
            = L.foldl' (\ i b -> (i `shiftL` 8) + fromIntegral b) 0 . BA.unpack
   |
39 |                 . BA.unpack
   |                   ^^^^^^^^^
```

Going off `master`, the latter issue in Annex/Balanced.hs has been resolved while Utility/Hash/Crypton.hs is still affected.

On a different note, I've tried building with botan-low, which failed to build due to the same issue above, i.e. Utility/Hash/Crypton.hs gets compiled even when using botan. I would expect that using botan would remove any use of crypton.

I like your work regarding the use of LLMs even in dependencies. I wasn't previously aware that there were already so many (and so widely used!) projects that included LLM generated code.
"""]]
